<sn><md>### Examples of Different Variables

```c
int age = 20;
float price = 99.5;
char grade = 'A';
double pi = 3.14159;
```

| Data Type | Variable | Stored Value |
| --------- | -------- | ------------ |
| `int`     | `age`    | `20`         |
| `float`   | `price`  | `99.5`       |
| `char`    | `grade`  | `'A'`        |
| `double`  | `pi`     | `3.14159`    |
</md></sn><sn><md>### Multiple Variable Declaration

Instead of 

```c
int a;
int b;
int c;
```

We can declare multiple variables of the **same type** by using (,) comma:

```c
int a, b, c;
```

You can also initialize them:

```c
int a = 10, b = 20, c = 30;
```

